{"name":"Mesa Verde","hex":"#7f976c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Mesa Verde","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A census-designated place in Riverside County, California, United States.","A portion of the Colorado Plateau in the United States that extends through parts of New Mexico, Colorado, and Utah, and is bounded by the San Juan River to the south, the Piedra River to the east, the San Juan Mountains to the north, and the Colorado River to the west."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mesa_Verde"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mesa Verde (Costa Mesa)","blocks":[{"text":"Mesa Verde is a neighborhood in Costa Mesa, California. It is bounded by the Interstate 405 freeway to the north, Harbor Boulevard to the east, Victoria Street to the south, and the Santa Ana River to the west. The community is bisected by Adams Avenue and contains the Fairview Channel, a Santa Ana River tributary that connects to Fairview Park, a wetland and riparian natural area. The neighborhood is home to two golf course complexes–the Costa Mesa Golf Course and the Mesa Verde Country Club."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesa_Verde_(Costa_Mesa)","wikidata":"Q105102674"},{"title":"Mesa Verde National Park","blocks":[{"text":"Mesa Verde National Park is a national park of the United States and UNESCO World Heritage Site located in Montezuma County, Colorado, and the only World Heritage Site in Colorado. The park protects some of the best-preserved Ancestral Puebloan ancestral sites in the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Cliff_Palace-Colorado-Mesa_Verde_NP.jpg/330px-Cliff_Palace-Colorado-Mesa_Verde_NP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesa_Verde_National_Park","wikidata":"Q237128"},{"title":"Mesa","blocks":[{"text":"A mesa is an isolated, flat-topped elevation, ridge, or hill, bounded from all sides by steep escarpments and standing distinctly above a surrounding plain. Mesas consist of flat-lying soft sedimentary rocks, such as shales, capped by a resistant layer of harder rock, like sandstone or limestone, forming a caprock that protects the flat summit. The caprock may also include dissected lava flows or eroded duricrust."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Over_Monument_Valley%2C_Navajo_Nation.jpg/330px-Over_Monument_Valley%2C_Navajo_Nation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesa","wikidata":"Q623319"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Glyptodon_old_drawing.jpg/500px-Glyptodon_old_drawing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Glyptodon_old_drawing.jpg/500px-Glyptodon_old_drawing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Paleo-Indians hunting a glyptodont, by Heinrich Harder c. 1920","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGlyptodon_old_drawing.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Barrier_Canyon_style%2C_Sego_Canyon.jpg/500px-Barrier_Canyon_style%2C_Sego_Canyon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Barrier_Canyon_style%2C_Sego_Canyon.jpg/1280px-Barrier_Canyon_style%2C_Sego_Canyon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Barrier_Canyon_style%2C_Sego_Canyon.jpg/500px-Barrier_Canyon_style%2C_Sego_Canyon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Archaic pictographs, c. 2500 BC, Sego Canyon, Utah","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarrier_Canyon_style%2C_Sego_Canyon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://th